title: Genesis 10 – The Nations of Men
description: A study in Genesis 10: the seventy nations descended from the three sons of Noah, and the God who sets the bounds of their habitation.
output: lessons/genesis/genesis-10-table-of-nations.html

=== Introduction
--- The Nations of Men [title]
overline: A study in Genesis 10
sub: The division of man into nations, from the three sons of Noah.
refs: Genesis 10:1; Genesis 10:32
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any reference to read the verse.

--- Races and nations
big: Genesis 10:32 | mark: by these were the nations divided in the earth after the flood
p: And so we have the division of man into races and nations. 70 different ethnic tribes, descended from the three sons of Noah. God commanded them to be fruitful and replenish the earth. [[Genesis 9:1]]

=== The three sons
--- The sons of Japheth
scripture: Genesis 10:2-5 | mark: every one after his tongue, after their families, in their nations
note: Among them Ashkenaz, of Japheth, not of Shem. [[Genesis 10:3]]

--- The sons of Ham
scripture: Genesis 10:6-14
p: Of Ham came Cush, Mizraim, Phut and Canaan, and of Cush, Nimrod: “a mighty hunter before the {Lord},” and the beginning of his kingdom was Babel. [[lesson:genesis-11-tower-of-babel|Genesis 11]]

--- Canaan
scripture: Genesis 10:15-20 | mark: the border of the Canaanites
center: The sons of Canaan, the nations whose land would be given to Abram’s seed, cursed in Genesis 9. [[Genesis 9:25]] [[Genesis 15:18-21]]

--- The sons of Shem
scripture: Genesis 10:21-25 | mark: for in his days was the earth divided
scripture: Genesis 10:26-31
note: Peleg: “for in his days was the earth divided.” We will see why in Genesis 11.

=== What the lists tell us
--- The lists of names
lead: I won’t lie, when the Bible gets into lists of names, I glaze over. But genealogies tell me things.
panel: History | Scripture is a historical account of man.
panel: God sets the bounds | God sets the nations and their borders and the habitations thereof. [[Acts 17:26]] [[Deuteronomy 32:8]]
panel-warn: God judges nations | God judges nations of men on earth, blessing them, cursing them, and at times erasing them. [[Jeremiah 18:7-10]]

--- One world government
big: Genesis 11:9 | mark: scatter them abroad upon the face of all the earth
p: When the nations unite under a one world government of men, they challenge God. And so God scatters them.
note: Much has been made of this account, and conclusions drawn from the curse of Canaan through Ham, Ashkenaz being of Japheth, not Shem, and so on. The speculation of men like Josephus and later historians, tracing the migration of the 70 original nations to today, is very popular. Have at it.

=== Close
--- God set the bounds [title]
overline: Genesis 10
point: A record of history | The nations of men really descend from the three sons of Noah.
point: God divides the nations | He determines the times before appointed and the bounds of their habitation. [[Acts 17:26]]
point: God judges nations | He blesses, curses and erases them, and scatters them when they unite against Him.

